                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/1273: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-07T15:00:00-05:00">November 7, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>382. Your 961, November 5, 5 p.m. The Legation may follow its judgment in regard
                    to method of seeking a satisfactory settlement of this question provided the
                    arrangement ultimately agreed to shall involve no concessions to Chinese
                    supervision greater than those indicated in the Department’s telegram of October
                    28, 2 p.m. Keep Department informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
